For case (a), we obtain $q=-14, p=8$ and hence $(x-p)(x-13)+4=(x-14)(x-17)$;
For case (b), we obtain $q=-12, p=8$ and hence $(x-p)(x-13)+4=(x-9)(x-12)$;
For case (c), we obtain $q=-15, p=17$ and hence $(x-p)(x-13)+4=(x-15)^{2}$; which is NOT what we want;
For case (d), we obtain $q=-11, p=9$ and hence $(x-p)(x-13)+4=(x-11)^{2}$; which is also NOT what we want. Hence the two possible values of $p$ are 8 and 18 , the sum of which is 26 .

